For example, online communities benefit from becoming more welcoming, as every time users cooperate by positively interacting with each other, they slightly impact the next user's behavior thus encouraging more cooperation~\cite{gonzalez2011dynamics,kang2015rise}.
Conversely, those who buy in a Ponzi scheme or in a speculative bubble amplify the illusion of profitability for other prospective buyers, thereby increasing the incentive to defect, i.e., to cash out, for those selling overvalued assets~\cite{kaizoji2000speculative}. In both examples, strategic interactions themselves reshape their own payoff structures.
