The choice of a \textit{Prisoner’s Dilemma} as the target game in the model represents a dynamics where defection is promoted. As the fraction of cooperators $\rho$ increases, the parameters are pushed towards the PD region. As a paradigmatic scenario, assume the PD with $D^T_r, D^T_g = 1$ is the target game: eq.~\ref{generaldeltapayoff} admits only one stable solution in $[0,1]$.
The results for each of the classes of baseline $G_B$ social dilemmas (different from the target) are now examined and depicted in Fig.~\ref{fig:PDtarget_game} and Fig.~\ref{fig:PDtarget_rho}
. 
When $G_B$ is in the \textit{Harmony Game} region, the dynamics hinders cooperation, reaching a stable state $\rho^* \in (0,1)$ with a feedback-driven game $G_{eq}$ belonging to one of two different social dilemma classes, depending on the relative value of the baseline parameters. For $D_r < D_g$, $G_{eq}$ is in the SD class, where $\rho^*$ is the expected mixed equilibrium. For $D_r > D_g$, $G_{eq}$ lies in the SH class and $\rho^*$ is a mixed equilibrium, deviating from the expected bistability: this behavior is at odds with EGT results, as a static SH game leads for any $\rho_0$ to an absorbing state (see Fig.\ref{schematic_game_result} for a stylized representation of this \textit{Chimera game} setting). 
Such a stable equilibrium can be mapped to the one found via EGT principles from yet another class of game $G^C$ (i.e. SD), whose parameters are found by solving \mbox{$\rho^* = D^C_r/(D^C_r -D^C_g) = \rho|_{\Delta \Pi = 0}$} as function of the baseline parameters.

If $G_B$ is a  \textit{Stag Hunt},
the only stable state is full defection, $\rho^* = 0$, therefore $G_{eq} = G_B$. Notably, this implies the loss of bistability which is typical of SH games in EGT. Finally, for $G_B$ as  a \textit{Snowdrift Game}, the stable state is $0<\rho^*<1$, and $G_{eq}$ is shifted from  $G_B$ but still belongs to the SD class. %SD is thus robust under the penalties for cooperation introduced by our model, as the nature of the social dilemma defining the environment is unchanged. 
