\subsection{Data processing and statistics}
% ----------------------------- %
The in silico experiments were, for the most part, case-based by simulating signals and calculating and presenting various metrics, e.g., separability, false positive rate, false negative rate, energy similarity, PNR, SIL, etc. We also performed statistical tests regarding the correlation between various metrics using Pearson's linear correlation coefficient (see Section~\ref{sec:quality_source_metric} and \ref{sec:results_population}). The simulations, decompositions and data processing were performed using MATLAB, where the source code to regenerate the results and figures is available in a git repository \citep{KlotzRohlen2025}.

