Similarly, implied values for $p_m$ are computed via
\begin{equation}\label{eq:IPd}
p_m^{(\text{imp})}(T_i,K_j) = \argmin_{0 \le p_m \le 1-p_{d,t}^{(r)}}
	 \left (
		\frac{G^{(\text{th})} \left( S_0,T_i,K_j;\sigma_t^{(r)}, \mu_t^{(r)} , p_{d,t}^{(r)}, p_m, r_{f,t} \right)
			- G^{(\text{emp})}(S_0,T_i,K_j) }
			{G^{(\text{emp})}(S_0,T_i,K_j)}
	\right )^2 ,
\end{equation}
from which we can compute the values
$$
	p_u | p_m^{(\text{imp})} (T_i,K_j) = 1  - p_{d,t}^{(r)} - p_m^{(\text{imp})}(T_i,K_j).
$$
