In contrast, if we have Poisson level statistics:
\begin{equation}
\left.\left\langle \cos\left[\qtheta(t)\right]\right\rangle\right\rvert_{\text{Poisson}} \approx \frac{t_{\htime}^2}{t_{\htime}^2+4\pi^2 t^2}.
\end{equation}
While this again starts off at $1$ at $t=0$, it never decays to negative values, and always remains positive. Thus, even in this coarse grained sense, the dynamics of the wavepacket under a Poisson spectrum remains close to the initial state at $\qtheta=0$ and does not shift towards the opposite side with $\qtheta=\pi$.

