    Two-point statistics of tracers of a fixed density~$\delta$ from a negative binomial distribution, a Poisson distribution, and a binomial distribution.
    \emph{Top panel:} The angular power spectra~$C_\ell$ of the simulated maps show the apparently different `shot noise' in each realisation.
    \emph{Middle panel:} The angular power spectra~$C_\ell$ measured from the sampled catalogue reveal that the bias returns to the `Poissonian' value beyond the simulated scales (\emph{hatched}).
