\end{equation*}
where $\mathcal{L}$ denotes the original loss function, $\lambda$ is the regularization strength (a hyperparameter of the network), and $||\mathscr{W}||^{2}$ represents the squared Frobenius norm of the weight matrices, that is, the sum of the squares of all trainable weight values in the network. For this experiment, we maintain the original network configuration (MNIST task with the tanh activation function and just one hidden layer). 


