Now consider $n=4$. Recall that $\F^{F84}_4\cap\Z_4$ is a 55-dimensional linear space containing $\E^{F84}_4$, see \Cref{prop:quartet-eqF84}. To prove equality, it is enough to show that there exist 55 linearly independent points in $CV_{T_{12}}^{F84}\cup CV_{T_{13}}^{F84}\cup CV_{T_{14}}^{F84}$.

Consider the diagonal matrix $D=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_1,\lambda_2,\lambda_4,\lambda_4)$, and for $i\in\lbrace 1,2,4\rbrace$, let $D_i$ be the specialization to $\lambda_i=1$ and $\lambda_j=0$, for $j\neq i$.
