It is evident that, in the case of nonlinear control, the incorporation of the reset element facilitates an increase in loop gain at low frequencies while maintaining the bandwidth and phase margin consistent with those of the linear control system.

However, thus far in this section, only the first-order SIDF characteristics of the reset element have been presented. In the subsequent sections, we will analyze the nonlinear control case based on the closed-loop higher-order SIDFs, aiming to minimize their impact on system performance.
