    L_2(s)=\frac{1+\frac{s}{\omega_x}}{1+\frac{s}{\omega_f}}
\end{equation}
with $\omega_r\leq\omega_x\leq\omega_f$. It can be shown that $C_{\mathrm{lead}}(s)=L_1(s)L_2(s)$, which by having $\omega_x=\omega_r$ it results in GFORE-$C_{\mathrm{lead}}$ structure and for $\omega_x=\omega_f$ it results in $C_{\mathrm{lead}}$-GFORE structure.
