{\bf Abstract.}
We construct  new sets of log-canonical coordinates on $SL(2)$ character varieties of unpunctured Riemann surfaces. These coordinates are obtained by combining the  shear coordinates  with length-twist type coordinates of Fenchel-Nielsen type and their extensions in complex domain.


\vskip1.0cm



 %   While Fock-Goncharov coordinates are well understood and studied for the $ SL(2, \mathbb{R}) $ character variety associated to punctured Riemann surfaces no such a formalism is available in the unpunctured case. The goal of this paper is to fulfill this gap. The presented solution consists to cut the reference Riemann surface of genus $g$ without punctures along an homologically trivial separating curve, parametrize each obtained piece by Fock-Goncharov coordinates and then glue them back while imposing constraints corresponding to matching perimeters and toric reduction. This procedure can be refined by cutting the reference surface along several (general) separating curves ; allowing one to arbitrarily "replace" Fock-Goncharov coordinates by toric ones. For the maximal case where the pieces correspond to the pairs of pants decomposition the relationship with Fenchel-Nielsen coordinates is discussed. %Finally we also describe in our setting an extension by attaching almost tight pairs of pants to geodesic boundaries in order to characterize psi-classes.


