 The number of edges of $\t\Gamma$ and  $\Gh$ equals $\t n=6\t\g-3$ and $\h n=6\h\g-3$, respectively.  The valences  of the vertices $\t v$ and $\h v$  equal to $2\t n$ and $2\h n$, respectively (since every edge of $\Gt$ (resp. $\Gh$) comes to $\t v$ (resp. $\h v$) twice).


