 The   form $\Omega$  on $V_g$ can be written as follows in terms of  coordinates (\ref{coo1})
(\ref{coo1}): 
\be
  \Omega= \Omega_0+ \t{\Omega}_{1}+\h{\Omega}_{1}+ \t{\Omega}_{2}+ \h{\Omega}_{2}
  \la{WPint}
  \ee
where 
\be
\Omega_{0}=2\mathrm{d}\len_\gamma \wedge \mathrm{d}\beta_\gamma\;,
\la{ltint}
\ee
\be
 \t{\Omega}_{1}= \sum_{\substack{i,j=2 \\ i<j} }^{6g_1-3} \left(\t c_{ij}-\t c_{1j}+\t c_{1i} \right)\mathrm{d}\zt_i\wedge \mathrm{d} \zt_j\;,\hskip0.7cm
\h{\Omega}_{1}=\sum_{\substack{k,l=2 \\ k<l} }^{6g_2-3} \left( \h c_{kl}-\h c_{1l}+\h c_{1k}\right) \mathrm{d}\zh_k \wedge \mathrm{d}\zh_l;,
\la{ossint}
\ee
\be
 \t{\Omega}_{2}=\frac{1}{2} \sum_{m=2}^{6g_1-3} \h c_{1m}  \mathrm{d}\len_\gamma \wedge \mathrm{d}\zt_m\;,\hskip0.7cm
