 K_{[123]}= M_{\alpha_1} M_{\beta_1}^{-1} M_{\alpha_1}^{-1} \;\dots \;.$$


\begin{prop}
    The form $ \Omega(\Gamma_0)$ given by (\ref{OmegaSt}) coincides with the Goldman  symplectic form $\Omega$ on $V_g$.
\end{prop}
\begin{proof}
  %  The Weil-Petersson form is the symplectic form which is an inverse of the Goldman form on $SL(2,\R)$ character variety of $\pi_1(\Ccal)$ \cite{wolpert1985weil}.
   The symplectic form $\Omega$ inverting the Goldman bracket on the $SL(N)$ character variety of $\pi_1(\Ccal)$ was computed by
    Alekseev and Malkin \cite{alekseev1995symplectic}. The form of  \cite{alekseev1995symplectic} can be represented via  (\ref{OmegaG}) for a special graph $G$ and the   jump matrices \cite{bertola2023extended}. In turns out that the Alekseev-Malkin graph can be transformed to the standard graph $\Gcal_0$ by a series of admissible moves preserving the symplectic form.  Therefore,  the form $\Omega(\Gamma_0)$ coincides with the Goldman symplectic form (for an arbitrary $SL(N)$ case).


\end{proof}



